# round-33: a String ctor takes at most ONE content/capacity source — a
# single positional arg (content or capacity) OR cap=, optionally combined
# with alloc=. Multi-source shapes used to slip past typecheck (only the
# 1-arg positional form was validated) and fall past the GIR String intercept
# into a call to an undefined `String` symbol — an unintelligible cc error
# ("incompatible types when assigning to type 'Str' from type 'int64_t'") /
# llc error ("'%v9' defined with type 'i64' but expected 'ptr'"). Must be a
# clean type error at `gg check` (Core #8).
void main():
    String s = String("a", "b")
    String t = String("a", cap=4)
    print(s)
    print(t)
